#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Verify that macOS bundles are portable universal binaries.
#
# Used by the universal macOS builds of the Justfile (`just macos-universal`,
# `just macos-test`) only. Regular single-architecture builds via build.sh are
# allowed to link against Homebrew and are not checked.
#
# Every Mach-O file found within the given bundles must
#   - contain both an arm64 and an x86_64 slice,
#   - require at most the given macOS version (minos) in every slice,
#   - only link against libraries shipped with macOS (/System/Library,
#     /usr/lib) or contained in the bundle itself,
#   - not carry an rpath pointing outside of the bundle, and
#   - have a valid code signature (Apple Silicon refuses to run unsigned code;
#     modifying a binary after linking invalidates its signature).
# Application bundles additionally have to declare the minimum macOS version
# in their Info.plist (LSMinimumSystemVersion). Without it, older systems refuse
# to start the app with a generic error message.
#
# Usage:
#   check_macos_portable <macos-target> <bundle> [<bundle> ...]
#
# Exits non-zero if any bundle violates one of the rules above.
#
